{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The low-latency TV transmitter and headphones feel like useful next choices because they would add wireless listening to the streaming and television setup I already use.",
    "The router and range extender relate to my streaming devices and security cameras, so their potential uses make sense even though I do not currently have a connection problem to solve."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The specialized speaker adapter, USB-C adapter, and AirPods cover depend on equipment or connection needs that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "Another Fire TV Stick repeats something I already own, while the HDMI cable and six short Ethernet cables do not address an immediate need. Being compatible with a home electronics setup is not enough for me to choose them now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in home electronics seems to have been extended too broadly to accessories without a clear connection to how I use my devices.",
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to offer another streaming stick, even though they also suggest that streaming is already covered."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more interested in adding a useful capability, such as wireless TV listening with little audio delay, than in duplicating equipment I already have.",
    "Networking equipment and cables become appealing when they solve a specific coverage or connection problem; owning several connected devices does not establish that I have one."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my home streaming and camera interests, but often miss the difference between a useful addition, a duplicate, and an accessory I have no current reason to buy."
}"}
